  "articleBody": "Converting a garage into usable living quarters gives your household extra room without building an expensive home addition. However, cutting corners during the planning phase leads to uncomfortable rooms and costly corrections later.\n\nCommon Mistakes to Avoid:\n- Skipping building permits: Treating a habitable conversion as cosmetic can lead to inspection failures or resale complications. Always confirm local approvals before demolition.\n- Ignoring floor moisture: Concrete slabs naturally transfer ground dampness. Laying finished flooring without a tested moisture barrier leads to warped materials and mold.\n- Inadequate thermal insulation: Garages have minimal exterior insulation. Skimping on wall and ceiling insulation makes the room freezing during cold months.\n- Neglecting emergency egress: Turning a garage into a legal bedroom requires proper egress windows or doors that meet residential safety codes.\n- Overlooking structural modifications: Swapping garage overhead doors for exterior walls or framing new door openings requires proper lintels and load-bearing support.\n\nWorking with an experienced finish contractor prevents these oversights from derailing your investment. At HH Remodeling LLC, we handle custom framing, drywall, and finish carpentry to build spaces that last. Contact Abraham at 303-505-0866 to review your conversion plans.",
  "datePublished": "2026-10-23"
